{
  "abstract": "Formalization of incremental n × n Latin squares and cyclic incremental n × n Latin squares representing n + 1 solutions of (n, c)-coins problems simultaneously for all 0 ≤ c ≤ n. We prove that (1) for every n ≥ 4, any incremental n × n Latin square represents valid (n, c)-coins solutions for all 0 ≤ c ≤ n simultaneously via value thresholding, and (2) for every n ≥ 4 with n ∉ {4, 6}, there exists a column permutation p such that the cyclic Latin square L(i, j) = (i + p(j)) mod n is incremental, using an injective-majorization principle across four infinite modular families modulo 6 and the four exceptional dimensions n ∈ {8, 9, 15, 21}, together with explicit non-cyclic incremental Latin squares for n = 4 and n = 6.",
